id: multiple-arms
name: Multiple Arms
kind: state
# A Special State (the user's terminology): no Narrative Requirement - only an effect that gives it enters it.
specialState: true
description: >
  More arms: more Weapons in hand, more answers, more blows before they tire.
text: >
  (1)-[Passive]: You can wield up to 4 Weapons simultaneously.

  (2)-[Triggered]: Upon entering this State or at the start of each Combat Round, gain an
  additional Counter Action to spend this Combat Round.

  (3)-[Triggered, 1/Round]: If you hit an Opponent with a Physical Attack, apply additional
  stack(s) of Diminishing Defense as if they were targeted by an additional Attacking Maneuver.

  (4)-[Triggered, 1/Round]: If you use an Attacking Maneuver of the Combination Profile, you
  may roll your Strike Roll an additional time.

  (5)-[1/Round]: You can spend 2 Counter Actions to use the Basic Attack Maneuver as an
  Instant Maneuver.

  (6)-[Passive]: Diminishing Offense doesn't apply until after your 4th Attacking Maneuver
  during each Combat Round.

---

# (2) is a Counter Action more for every Round spent in it, the one it is entered in included: the
# Counter Actions are counted against what is spent this Round, so one more is there at once.
#
# (3), (4) and (5) are once a Combat Round, each counted on its own - `round:multiple-arms.*` among
# the uses a new Round hands back (chat.mjs ARMS_USES). (3) and (4) are Triggered: the player's to
# use or not, so each is a button - (3) a card offered on a Physical hit, (4) "Roll 4: Multiple Arms"
# beside Combination's own (one more follow-up, like Alotta Lotta Attacks) - and nothing is spent
# until it is pressed. (5) is the "Instant" button on the Basic Attack's row.
[passive]
weapons.wielded min= 4;
actions.counter += 1;
diminishing.defense.onPhysicalHit = true;
combination.extraRoll = true;
basicAttack.asInstant = true;
attacks.free min= 4;
